; The example program from the nanochess/bootLogo README (BSD-2-Clause,
; (c) 2024 Oscar Toledo G.), one REPL line per source line. bootLogo matches
; only two letters of a procedure name; Glyph uses whole names, which this
; program already does. Output is a text-cell rendering, not CGA pixels.
TO CURVE REPEAT 4 [LT 10 FD 10] END
TO PETAL [CURVE LT 140 CURVE] END
TO FLOWER REPEAT 4 [PETAL LT 50] END
FLOWER
RT 180
FD 50
RT 140
PETAL
PU
FD 50
